{"2313780": {"success": true, "data": {"type": "game", "name": "Bad Dream: Purgatory", "steam_appid": 2313780, "required_age": 0, "is_free": false, "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Bad Dream: Purgatory</strong> is a surreal point and click game set in an abandoned and forgotten project, filled with unused characters from a cancelled game. These characters are trapped in a state of limbo, suspended in nothingness without any purpose or direction. It's up to you to decide their fate and give them the meaning they so desperately crave. &quot;You can't die if you've never lived&quot; - but what if you only exist as a first thought, a person without any depth?</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Unlike previous Bad Dream games, Purgatory is presented in a side-scrolling format giving players a more immersive and personal experience. The artstyle is simplistic, with hand-drawn illustrations that perfectly capture the game's atmosphere.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Important:</strong>  The game has a full Point &amp; Click mode with a static camera.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The game consists of three chapters. Two of them (the introductory one and the simplified ending) are linear. The open world is non-linear and includes all achievements and a &quot;true ending.&quot;</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Game Features:</strong></p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >A non-linear chapter allowing you to hunt for secrets and achievements</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Two modes of gameplay (side-scrolling or static camera)</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Interactive environment</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Sound environments - SFX sound different in different rooms (echo, muffled sound, etc.)</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Custom music and sound effects ( I learned how to compose my own music and I bought a microphone to record my own SFX )</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Artstyle - I learned how to draw as well :P</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >A game made by one person - Guys. I even drew my own fonts :P To be fair I wasn't able to record ALL SFX myself, but other than that I made this game alone. <strong>Btw. NO AI</strong></p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >This is version 2.0, released in July 2026. It includes a multitude of changes, improvements, and fixes. The biggest one is the switch from 2.5D to side-scrolling mode.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>(The first version is still available for download as the &quot;old version&quot; - tutorial in the pinned post)</strong>  </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p>", "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Bad Dream: Purgatory</strong> is a surreal point and click game set in an abandoned and forgotten project, filled with unused characters from a cancelled game. These characters are trapped in a state of limbo, suspended in nothingness without any purpose or direction. It's up to you to decide their fate and give them the meaning they so desperately crave. &quot;You can't die if you've never lived&quot; - but what if you only exist as a first thought, a person without any depth?</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Unlike previous Bad Dream games, Purgatory is presented in a side-scrolling format giving players a more immersive and personal experience. The artstyle is simplistic, with hand-drawn illustrations that perfectly capture the game's atmosphere.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Important:</strong>  The game has a full Point &amp; Click mode with a static camera.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The game consists of three chapters. Two of them (the introductory one and the simplified ending) are linear. The open world is non-linear and includes all achievements and a &quot;true ending.&quot;</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Game Features:</strong></p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >A non-linear chapter allowing you to hunt for secrets and achievements</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Two modes of gameplay (side-scrolling or static camera)</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Interactive environment</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Sound environments - SFX sound different in different rooms (echo, muffled sound, etc.)</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Custom music and sound effects ( I learned how to compose my own music and I bought a microphone to record my own SFX )</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Artstyle - I learned how to draw as well :P</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >A game made by one person - Guys. I even drew my own fonts :P To be fair I wasn't able to record ALL SFX myself, but other than that I made this game alone. <strong>Btw. NO AI</strong></p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >This is version 2.0, released in July 2026. It includes a multitude of changes, improvements, and fixes. The biggest one is the switch from 2.5D to side-scrolling mode.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>(The first version is still available for download as the &quot;old version&quot; - tutorial in the pinned post)</strong>  </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p>", "short_description": "Explore a surreal landscape filled with unused characters from a cancelled project. Will you give them purpose, or will they be doomed to suffer?", "supported_languages": "English, Polish", "header_image": "https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2313780/9dde618f24fc9af281d777ffb928f406d58772be/header.jpg?t=1784815106", "capsule_image": "https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2313780/aa2ee9c7bbe89270cd7b2fd17d3ebdec3ff7704f/capsule_2